<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
  <title>Climate Change 2023: IPCC AR6 Synthesis Report - Infographic</title>
  <style>
    * { margin: 0; padding: 0; box-sizing: border-box; }
    html, body { width: 100%; height: 100%; background: #0a1628; }
    #container { width: 100%; height: 100%; min-height: 900px; }
    #export-btn {
      position: fixed; top: 16px; right: 16px; z-index: 999;
      background: #e84e1b; color: #fff; border: none;
      padding: 10px 20px; border-radius: 6px; font-size: 14px;
      cursor: pointer; font-family: sans-serif;
    }
    #export-btn:hover { background: #c43a10; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <button id="export-btn">Export SVG</button>
  <div id="container"></div>
  <script src="/app/vendor/infographic.min.js"></script>
  <script>
    const syntax = `infographic sequence-roadmap-vertical-simple
data
  title Climate Change 2023: IPCC AR6 Synthesis Report Key Findings
  desc Human-caused climate change is unequivocal, accelerating, and the window for meaningful action is rapidly closing.
  sequences
    - label OBSERVED CHANGES & CURRENT STATE
      desc +1.1°C global temperature rise (2011–2020 vs. 1850–1900) · CO₂ at 410 ppm — highest in 2 million years · Global GHG emissions ~59 GtCO₂e (2019) · Sea level rose ~0.20 m (1901–2018) · Arctic September sea ice area down ~40% (1979–2020). Every region has experienced more frequent and intense extreme weather events directly attributable to human influence.
    - label FUTURE PROJECTIONS ACROSS SSP SCENARIOS
      desc SSP1-1.9 (Very Low): ~1.4°C by 2100 | SSP1-2.6 (Low): ~1.8°C | SSP2-4.5 (Intermediate): ~2.7°C | SSP3-7.0 (High): ~3.6°C | SSP5-8.5 (Very High, fossil-fuel intensive): ~4.4°C. Sea level rise projected 0.28–0.55 m (SSP1-1.9) to 0.63–1.01 m (SSP5-8.5) by 2100, with further rise locked in for centuries regardless of pathway.
    - label RISKS, VULNERABILITIES & CASCADING IMPACTS
      desc 3.3–3.6 billion people live in contexts highly vulnerable to climate change. Over 50% of global population faces severe water scarcity at least 1 month/year. Up to 14% of terrestrial species at very high extinction risk at 1.5°C. Food security: crop yield growth slowing; fisheries declining in tropics. Heat mortality and vector-borne disease ranges expanding globally.
    - label MITIGATION & ADAPTATION PATHWAYS
      desc To limit warming to 1.5°C: reduce GHG emissions 43% below 2019 levels by 2030 and reach net-zero CO₂ by ~2050. For 2°C: 27% reduction by 2030, net-zero CO₂ by ~2070. Remaining carbon budget from 2020 for 50% chance of 1.5°C: ~500 GtCO₂. Key levers: decarbonize energy, electrify transport, efficiency gains, protect carbon sinks.
    - label THE NARROWING WINDOW FOR ACTION
      desc Decisions made this decade determine whether 1.5°C or 2°C is achievable. Delayed action raises costs, locks in high-carbon infrastructure, and reduces feasibility. Climate finance falls short by 3–6× for adaptation alone. Immediate, deep, and sustained emissions reductions across ALL sectors are essential to secure a liveable future.
theme
  palette #1e3a5f #c0392b #e67e22 #f39c12 #e74c3c`;

    const infographic = new AntVInfographic.Infographic({
      container: '#container',
      width: '100%',
      height: '100%',
    });

    infographic.render(syntax);

    document.fonts?.ready.then(() => {
      infographic.render(syntax);
    }).catch((err) => console.error('Font load error:', err));

    document.getElementById('export-btn').addEventListener('click', async () => {
      try {
        const svgDataUrl = await infographic.toDataURL({ type: 'svg' });
        const a = document.createElement('a');
        a.href = svgDataUrl;
        a.download = 'ipcc-ar6-infographic.svg';
        a.click();
      } catch (e) {
        console.error('Export failed:', e);
        alert('Export failed: ' + e.message);
      }
    });
  </script>
</body>
</html>
