data
  title Climate Change 2023: IPCC AR6 Synthesis Report — Key Findings
  desc The most comprehensive climate assessment to date. Human-caused climate change is unequivocal, accelerating, and the window for meaningful action is rapidly closing. Source: IPCC (2023)
  sequences
    - label Observed Warming: +1.1°C (2011–2020 vs. 1850–1900)
      desc CO₂ at 410 ppm — highest in 2 million years. Global GHG emissions ~59 GtCO₂e (2019). Sea level rose ~0.20 m since 1901. Arctic sea ice down ~40%. Every region hit by intensifying extremes attributable to human influence.
      icon thermometer
    - label 3.3–3.6 Billion People Exposed to Severe Climate Hazards
      desc Highly vulnerable to cascading climate risks. Over 50% of global population faces water scarcity at least 1 month/year. Biodiversity: up to 14% of terrestrial species face very high extinction risk at 1.5°C.
      icon person 3 fill
    - label SSP Projections: 1.4°C to 4.4°C Warming by 2100
      desc SSP1-1.9 (very low): ~1.4°C | SSP2-4.5 (intermediate): ~2.7°C | SSP5-8.5 (very high): ~4.4°C. Sea level rise 0.28–1.01 m. Every fraction of a degree matters for lives and ecosystems.
      icon chart line uptrend xyaxis
    - label 43% Emissions Cut Required by 2030
      desc To limit warming to 1.5°C, GHG must fall 43% below 2019 levels by 2030 and reach net-zero CO₂ by ~2050. For 2°C: 27% cut by 2030, net-zero by ~2070. Key levers: clean energy, transport, carbon sinks.
      icon arrow down circle fill
    - label ~500 GtCO₂ Carbon Budget Remaining — Act Now
