<div class="page">

  <!-- HEADER -->
  <div class="header">
    <div class="header-eyebrow">Intergovernmental Panel on Climate Change · AR6 Synthesis Report 2023</div>
    <div class="header-title">Climate Change <span>2023</span>:<br>Key Findings from the IPCC Sixth Assessment Report</div>
    <div class="header-subtitle">The most comprehensive scientific assessment of climate change to date — integrating findings from the physical science basis, impacts and adaptation, and mitigation across the AR6 cycle.</div>
    <div class="header-source">Source: IPCC, 2023. AR6 Synthesis Report: Climate Change 2023. Intergovernmental Panel on Climate Change.</div>
  </div>

  <!-- SECTION: HEADLINE METRICS -->
  <div class="section"><div class="section-label">Observed Changes &amp; Current State</div></div>
  <div class="metrics-grid">
    <div class="metric-card accent-red">
      <div class="metric-value">+1.1<span class="metric-unit">°C</span></div>
      <div class="metric-label">Global surface warming<br>2011–2020 vs. 1850–1900</div>
    </div>
    <div class="metric-card accent-orange">
      <div class="metric-value">410<span class="metric-unit"> ppm</span></div>
      <div class="metric-label">Atmospheric CO₂ in 2019<br>Highest in 2 million years</div>
    </div>
    <div class="metric-card accent-amber">
      <div class="metric-value">59<span class="metric-unit"> GtCO₂e</span></div>
      <div class="metric-label">Annual GHG emissions<br>(2019 baseline)</div>
    </div>
    <div class="metric-card accent-teal">
      <div class="metric-value">~0.20<span class="metric-unit">m</span></div>
      <div class="metric-label">Sea level rise since 1901<br>1901–2018 observed</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="divider" style="margin-top:20px;"></div>

  <!-- SECTION: SSP PROJECTIONS -->
  <div class="section"><div class="section-label">Future Projections — SSP Scenario Warming by 2100</div></div>
  <div class="chart-section">
    <div class="ssp-grid">
      <div class="ssp-row">
        <div class="ssp-label">SSP1-1.9<br><span style="font-size:9px;color:#5a7a99">Very Low</span></div>
        <div class="ssp-bar-track">
          <div class="ssp-bar ssp1"><span class="ssp-bar-desc">Sustainability focus</span>~1.4°C</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="ssp-row">
        <div class="ssp-label">SSP1-2.6<br><span style="font-size:9px;color:#5a7a99">Low</span></div>
        <div class="ssp-bar-track">
          <div class="ssp-bar ssp2"><span class="ssp-bar-desc">Low emissions</span>~1.8°C</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="ssp-row">
        <div class="ssp-label">SSP2-4.5<br><span style="font-size:9px;color:#5a7a99">Intermediate</span></div>
        <div class="ssp-bar-track">
          <div class="ssp-bar ssp3"><span class="ssp-bar-desc">Current policies</span>~2.7°C</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="ssp-row">
        <div class="ssp-label">SSP3-7.0<br><span style="font-size:9px;color:#5a7a99">High</span></div>
        <div class="ssp-bar-track">
          <div class="ssp-bar ssp4"><span class="ssp-bar-desc">Regional rivalry</span>~3.6°C</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="ssp-row">
        <div class="ssp-label">SSP5-8.5<br><span style="font-size:9px;color:#5a7a99">Very High</span></div>
        <div class="ssp-bar-track">
          <div class="ssp-bar ssp5"><span class="ssp-bar-desc">Fossil-fuel intensive</span>~4.4°C</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="ssp-axis">
      <span>0°C</span><span>1°C</span><span>2°C</span><span>3°C</span><span>4°C</span><span>4.4°C</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="divider" style="margin-top:20px;"></div>

  <!-- SECTION: RISKS & IMPACTS -->
  <div class="section"><div class="section-label">Risks, Vulnerabilities &amp; Cascading Impacts</div></div>
  <div class="impacts-grid">
    <div class="impact-card">
      <div class="impact-stat">3.3–3.6B</div>
      <div class="impact-title">People Exposed</div>
      <div class="impact-text">Living in contexts highly vulnerable to severe climate hazards — disproportionately in developing nations, small island states, and the Global South.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="impact-card">
      <div class="impact-stat">&gt;50%</div>
      <div class="impact-title">Water Scarcity</div>
      <div class="impact-text">Of global population faces severe water scarcity for at least one month per year. Droughts intensifying across subtropical regions.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="impact-card">
      <div class="impact-stat">14%</div>
      <div class="impact-title">Species at Risk</div>
      <div class="impact-text">Up to 14% of terrestrial species face very high extinction risk at 1.5°C. Biodiversity loss accelerates steeply at higher warming levels.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="impact-card">
      <div class="impact-stat">3–6×</div>
      <div class="impact-title">Finance Gap</div>
      <div class="impact-text">Climate finance falls 3–6× short of adaptation needs alone. Equity and finance are central to all viable mitigation pathways.</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="divider" style="margin-top:20px;"></div>

  <!-- SECTION: MITIGATION PATHWAY -->
  <div class="section"><div class="section-label">Mitigation Pathways — What Must Happen</div></div>
  <div class="steps-section">
    <div class="steps-list">

      <div class="step-row">
        <div class="step-connector">
          <div class="step-dot" style="background:#e74c3c">01</div>
          <div class="step-line"></div>
        </div>
        <div class="step-content">
          <div class="step-badge" style="background:rgba(231,76,60,0.15);color:#e74c3c;">Emissions Reduction</div>
          <div class="step-title">43% cut in GHG emissions by 2030</div>
          <div class="step-desc">Global GHG emissions must fall 43% below 2019 levels by 2030 to limit warming to 1.5°C. For a 2°C limit, a 27% reduction is required. Remaining carbon budget from 2020: ~500 GtCO₂ (50% chance of 1.5°C).</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="step-row">
        <div class="step-connector">
          <div class="step-dot" style="background:#c0392b">02</div>
          <div class="step-line"></div>
        </div>
        <div class="step-content">
          <div class="step-badge" style="background:rgba(192,57,43,0.15);color:#c0392b;">Net Zero Target</div>
          <div class="step-title">Net-zero CO₂ by ~2050 (1.5°C) or ~2070 (2°C)</div>
          <div class="step-desc">Rapid decarbonization of energy systems is the single largest lever. Electrification of transport and industry, demand-side efficiency improvements, and halting deforestation are all essential components.</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="step-row">
        <div class="step-connector">
          <div class="step-dot" style="background:#e67e22">03</div>
          <div class="step-line"></div>
        </div>
        <div class="step-content">
          <div class="step-badge" style="background:rgba(230,126,34,0.15);color:#e67e22;">Carbon Sinks</div>
          <div class="step-title">Protect and restore carbon sinks</div>
          <div class="step-desc">Forests, wetlands, and soils represent critical natural carbon sinks. Protection, restoration, and sustainable management of ecosystems must complement technological solutions. Negative emissions technologies (CDR) are required at scale.</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="step-row">
        <div class="step-connector">
          <div class="step-dot" style="background:#f39c12">04</div>
          <div class="step-line" style="background:transparent;"></div>
        </div>
        <div class="step-content">
          <div class="step-badge" style="background:rgba(243,156,18,0.15);color:#f39c12;">Adaptation</div>
          <div class="step-title">Scale-up adaptation across all vulnerable systems</div>
          <div class="step-desc">Water security, climate-resilient agriculture, coastal protection, health systems, and ecosystem-based adaptation are all needed simultaneously. Adaptation and mitigation reinforce each other — both are required.</div>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- CALL TO ACTION -->
  <div class="cta-section">
    <div class="cta-headline">The Narrowing Window — <em>The choices made this decade are decisive</em></div>
    <div class="cta-text">Every fraction of a degree of warming avoided reduces risk, saves lives, and preserves ecosystems. Delayed action raises costs, locks in high-carbon infrastructure, and diminishes the feasibility of 1.5°C or even 2°C. Immediate, deep, and sustained emissions reductions across all sectors are essential to secure a liveable and sustainable future for all.</div>
    <div class="cta-stats">
      <div>
        <div class="cta-stat-val">~500 GtCO₂</div>
        <div class="cta-stat-lbl">Carbon budget remaining<br>(50% chance, 1.5°C, from 2020)</div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="cta-stat-val">43%</div>
        <div class="cta-stat-lbl">Required emissions cut<br>by 2030 for 1.5°C pathway</div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="cta-stat-val">3.3–3.6B</div>
        <div class="cta-stat-lbl">People highly vulnerable<br>to severe climate hazards</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- FOOTER -->
  <div class="footer">
    <div class="footer-left">
      IPCC, 2023. AR6 Synthesis Report: Climate Change 2023.<br>
      Intergovernmental Panel on Climate Change. Geneva, Switzerland.<br>
      Data as of publication date. All warming values relative to 1850–1900 baseline.
    </div>
    <div class="footer-right">
      <div class="footer-badge">AR6 · SYR · 2023</div>
    </div>
  </div>

</div>

<button id="export-btn">Export SVG</button>
<script src="/app/vendor/infographic.min.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
