  <script>
    const syntax = `infographic list-column-vertical-icon-arrow
data
  title Climate Change 2023: IPCC AR6 Synthesis Report — Key Findings
  desc Human-caused climate change is unequivocal, accelerating, and the window for meaningful action is rapidly closing. Source: IPCC Sixth Assessment Report (2023)
  lists
    - label Observed Warming: +1.1°C Above Pre-Industrial Baseline
      desc Global surface temperature rose +1.1°C (2011–2020 vs. 1850–1900). Atmospheric CO₂ reached 410 ppm — the highest level in at least 2 million years. Sea level rose ~0.20 m since 1901. Arctic sea-ice area down ~40%. Every region on Earth has experienced more frequent and intense extreme weather attributable to human influence.
      icon thermometer
    - label 3.3–3.6 Billion People Exposed to Severe Climate Hazards
      desc Approximately half the world's population faces severe water scarcity for at least one month per year. Up to 14% of terrestrial species face very high extinction risk at 1.5°C. Food security is declining as crop yield growth slows and tropical fisheries shrink. Heat-related mortality and vector-borne diseases are expanding rapidly.
